                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which RoC office handles partnership to LLP conversion in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>The Registrar of Companies (RoC), NCT of Delhi and Haryana, located at 4th Floor, IFCI Tower, 61 Nehru Place, New Delhi - 110019 handles all LLP conversion filings. All filings are electronic through MCA V3 portal - no physical visit required. Patron's Delhi team files regularly with this office.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I get partnership to LLP conversion done online from Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes - the entire process is 100% online through the MCA V3 portal. Form 17, FiLLiP and Form 3 are all web-based forms filed electronically with digital signatures. The only physical element is the LLP agreement on Delhi e-stamp paper, which Patron handles through SHCIL e-stamping.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the partnership to LLP conversion fee in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Partnership to LLP conversion in Delhi costs from Rs 7,499 with Patron Accounting (all-inclusive). Government fees include Rs 200 for name reservation, Rs 500-5,000 for FiLLiP based on capital slab, and Delhi stamp duty at 1% of capital capped at Rs 5,000 - lower than Maharashtra's Rs 50,000 cap.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does partnership to LLP conversion take in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Typically 15-25 working days from document submission to Certificate of Incorporation. DSC procurement 1-2 days, name approval 2-4 days, RoC Delhi processing 5-10 working days. Post-incorporation compliance (Form 3, Form 14) runs in parallel. Patron's pre-screening minimises rejection risk.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can an unregistered partnership firm convert to LLP in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>No. Only firms registered under the Indian Partnership Act, 1932 are eligible under Section 55 of the LLP Act. Many Delhi trading firms in Chandni Chowk operate without registration. These must first register with the Registrar of Firms (2-4 additional weeks) before applying for conversion.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is stamp duty payable on property transfer during conversion?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>When assets vest in the LLP by operation of law under Schedule II of the LLP Act and no separate conveyance deed is executed, no additional stamp duty is payable. Only the LLP agreement stamp duty (1% of capital, max Rs 5,000 in Delhi) applies. Judicial precedent supports this position.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens to existing contracts after conversion?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Under Schedule II, Para 7 of the LLP Act, all contracts, agreements, employment arrangements, rights and obligations transfer to the LLP by operation of law. No new contracts needed. However, licences and permits (Delhi Shop Act, FSSAI, trade licence) must be separately updated.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
